SUMMARY:Ani DiFranco Concert // SOLD OUT //
DESCRIPTION:Ani DiFranco is bringing the Spirit of Love to Gundlach Bundschu Winery with Special Guest Valerie June – Presented by (((folkYeah!))) and Gundlach Bundschu on Sunday August 16\, 2026 at 6:30pm at the Gundlach Bundschu Amphitheater in Sonoma\, CA.\n\nWHEN: Sunday\, August 16th 2026 \nWHERE: GB Amphitheater \nTIME: Doors 5:30pm | Show 6:30pm \nBUY TICKETS\n// SOLD OUT // Pre-paid parking is still available to ticket holders. $20 at entry\, $16.50 pre-paid. Paid Parking is not required Bacchus club members and electric vehicle or carpooling with 3+. \nChildren 5 and under are free and do not require a ticket. For safety\, infants or babies in arms are not permitted. \n\nFood available for purchase (vendors will be announced prior to the show) \n  \nTICKETING:\nHave your ticket ready when you arrive! If you opted for mobile delivery\, please make sure it’s ready to go on your phone. Printed tickets? Have them out and ready to be scanned. Bacchus Club members\, enjoy express entry with your special line. \nPARKING:\nParking is complimentary for Bacchus Wine Club members. To encourage carpooling\, we offer free parking to vehicles with 3+ passengers\, full 2-seaters\, motorcycles\, and electric vehicles. Otherwise\, parking will be $16.50 pre-paid in advance or $20 (cash only) at entry. For ADA accommodations please let the parking attendant know. \nPLEASE NO:\n\nCoolers\nWater (bring an empty bottle as we have filtered re-fill stations)\nPets\nChairs with legs of any length (stadium seats that sit flat on the ground are permitted)\nOutside food or drink\nBad Attitudes… this is Rhinefarm after all\n\nACCESSIBILITY:\nFor any questions regarding ADA accommodations related to parking\, seating\, restrooms\, etc. please contact us at info@gunbun.com or 707.938.5277. \nYOUR EXPERIENCE\, YOUR ADVENTURE:\nAt Gundlach Bundschu Winery\, we invite you to immerse yourself in the magic of our historic Redwood Barn\, where the beauty of nature blends with unforgettable performances. As with all great adventures\, attending an outdoor event carries a touch of unpredictability. \nWhether it’s the rustle of the vines in the breeze\, the gentle slope of the hillside\, or the surprises nature has in store\, we encourage you to embrace the moment. While we strive to create a safe and enjoyable environment\, the great outdoors brings its own set of risks. By joining us\, you understand and accept the inherent possibilities\, but not limited to\, uneven ground\, changing weather\, and the occasional visit from our local wildlife. We ask that you tread carefully\, come prepared for all conditions\, and remember to look after yourself and your belongings. \nBy attending our events\, you acknowledge that your participation is voluntary\, and you assume all responsibility for any personal injuries\, accidents\, or loss of property that may occur during your time with us. Gundlach Bundschu Winery and its team are dedicated to your safety\, but cannot be held liable for incidents that may arise from the natural elements of this experience. \nIn purchasing a ticket and joining us under the open sky\, you agree to these terms and release Gundlach Bundschu Winery from any claims or liabilities associated with the inherent risks of an outdoor gathering. We look forward to sharing this special place with you\, where every moment is part of the journey. \nMAKE SURE TO VISIT OUR VENUE INFORMATION PAGE – HERE\nVENUE MAP
URL:https://www.gunbun.com/event/ani-difranco-concert/
LOCATION:GB Amphitheater\, 2000 Denmark St\, Sonoma\, CA\, 95476\, United States
CATEGORIES:Concert,Winery Event
